    "https://uscupstate.edu/employment/student-positions/": {
      "title": "Student Employment  Opportunities",
      "description": "Student Positions - USC Upstate Skip to content Visit Request Info Give Apply Employment SpartanHub Academics Admissions Student Experience Search for: Search for: About About the University Administration Campus Maps & Locations Campus Resources Community Faculty Governance Fast Facts Office of the Chancellor University Advancement Upstate Magazine Academics Academics at USC Upstate Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Academic Centers and Services Majors & Programs Our Colleges Upstate Online Continuing Education Study Abroad Admissions Admissions Overview First-Year Students Graduate Students Online Students Transfer Student International Students Non-Degree Seeking Adult Learners Admissions Resources Orientation Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Tuition and Fees Scholarships Residency FAFSA Student Financial Literacy Cost of Attendance Student Life Explore the Student Experience Campus and Facilities Get Involved Housing and Residential Life Student Services & Resources A-Z Index News Events Student Employment  Opportunities at USC Upstate Employment Student Positions In this section Employee Benefits Executive Search Faculty Positions Human Resources Staff Positions Student Positions + For Student Employment For Student Hire Representatives For Supervisors of Student Employees Student Employment Opportunities at USC Upstate On-campus employment provides valuable work experience and career-enhancing opportunities for a competitive job market after graduation. Many benefits exist for students who can balance the demands of work and school. Students who successfully manage classroom and employment commitments are much more likely to impress future employers. Working on campus or in the community also connects students with resources which may help them with challenges in and out of the classroom. Learn more about on-campus student employment . The Financial Aid office supports students regarding educational financial assistance. Federal work-study is awarded by the Financial Aid office. Students who have been awarded work-study must find a job on campus to earn the designated award. Career Services assists student and faculty with internships and post-graduation employment. When using the USC Jobs system , select “USC Upstate” as the campus to see all current vacancies for this University. View Job Openings Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. See the Job Reference and Background Checks policy (PDF) for more information. Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution The University of South Carolina is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Women, minorities, protected veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. The University of South Carolina Upstate has designated as the EEO Coordinator Dagmara Bruce, Human Resources Director, 800 University Way, Spartanburg, SC 29303, Phone: 864-503-5933. The University of South Carolina-Upstate has designated as the ADA Title II, Section 504, and Title IX Coordinator for USC Upstate campus Lyda Costello Kiser, Civil Rights and Title IX/Title IX & ADA Coordinator, 800 University Way, Library 117B, Spartanburg, SC 29303, Phone: 864-503-7193. USC Upstate participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/e-verify . About Student Life Admissions Athletics Financial Aid Alumni Academics USC Upstate Events USC Upstate News A-Z Index Visit Request Info Give Apply SpartanHub 800 University Way Spartanburg, SC 29303 864-503-5000 Employment Policies and Procedures Civil Rights & Title IX Report a Digital Accessibility Issue"
